# Committed readings for stream-typed-copy.wasm: a guest's copy of typed elements through its own stream (#1275, ADR 0124).
# Built:       wasm-tools parse stream-typed-copy.wat -o stream-typed-copy.wasm   (wasm-tools 1.258.0; validates --features all)
# Invocation:  wasmtime run -W component-model-async=y --invoke '<export>()' stream-typed-copy.wasm
# Engine:      wasmtime 49.0.3 (f96eabaa1 2026-10-14), .oracle/wasmtime-49.0.3/wasmtime, darwin/arm64.
# Runs:        10 of 10 per line, each identical.
#
# Each line is `<export>: <wasmtime's reading>`. A `pin <export>:` line is the pin's answer where it is not
# wasmtime's (ADR 0102: the pin defines the semantics), and the test asserts it instead.
u32-wf-result: 48
u32-wf-w0: 287454020
u32-wf-w1: 1432778632
u32-wf-w2: 2578103244
u32-wf-w3: 0
u32-rf-result: 48
u32-rf-w0: 287454020
u32-rf-w2: 2578103244
u32-rf-w3: 0
u32-partial-result: 32
u32-partial-w2: 0
u32-equal-type-result: 48
f32-wf-w0: 2143289345
pin f32-wf-w0: 2143289344
f32-wf-w1: 1069547520
f32-rf-w0: 2143289345
pin f32-rf-w0: 2143289344
f64-wf-lo: 1
pin f64-wf-lo: 0
f64-wf-hi: 2146959360
u8-wf-result: 48
u8-wf-w0: 2241348
#
# Meaning. `wf`: the write of 3 parks, then a read of 4 copies (the read is the second arriver). `rf`: the read of 4
# parks, then the write of 3 copies. The written words are 0x11223344, 0x55667788, 0x99aabbcc at 64; the reader's
# buffer is at 128.
#   *-result 48       COMPLETED (0) with progress 3, in elements: 3 << 4.
#   u32-*-w0..w2      the three words, each whole; w3 is 0, so no fourth element was written.
#   u32-partial       a read of 2: progress 2 (32), and the third word of the buffer is untouched.
#   u32-equal-type    the read names type 2, `stream u32` like the end's type 1: one type to the pin
#                     (def:copy:"trap_if(end.t != stream_or_future_t.t)" compares types, not indices).
#   f32-*-w0          the NaN 0x7fc00001. wasmtime preserves its payload (2143289345); the pin's lift
#                     canonicalises it under DETERMINISTIC_PROFILE (0x7fc00000, 2143289344) and randomises it
#                     otherwise, so wasmtime's reading is inside the pin's set. Burroughs takes the deterministic
#                     outcome, as future-self-copy-elems.reading's floats do.
#   f32-wf-w1         1.5 (0x3fc00000), unchanged.
#   f64-wf-lo/hi      the NaN 0x7ff8000000000001's two words: wasmtime keeps the low 1, the pin's deterministic
#                     outcome is 0x7ff8000000000000.
#   u8-wf-*           the control: 3 bytes, 0x44 0x33 0x22, progress 3.
#
# Burroughs before ADR 0124 (main at 7ffc135): every u32, f32 and f64 row is refused at its read, "canon
# stream.read of type 1, whose element is not one byte" (ADR 0123); the u8 rows agree.
